    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Quantification: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note:
This property is used to indicate the language encoded by the TX3 Writing System and used for writing, reading or rendering (i.e. transcribing) a TX1 Written Text.

Examples:
- The Latin alphabet (TX3), used to encode the identical inscriptions (TX1) on the Arch of Constantine, encodes the Latin language (E56) used to convey the message of the inscriptions.

In First Order Logic:
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ TX3(x)
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ E56(y)
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ P2(x,y)
</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="TXP6i_is_encoding_of">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TXP6i is encoding of</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation>TXP6i</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">is encoding of</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E56_Language"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="TX3_Writing_System"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="TXP6_encodes"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2i_is_type_of"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note of the inverse property:
This property is used to indicate the language encoded by the TX3 Writing System and used for writing, reading or rendering (i.e. transcribing) a TX1 Written Text.

Examples of the inverse property:
- The Latin alphabet (TX3), used to encode the identical inscriptions (TX1) on the Arch of Constantine, encodes the Latin language (E56) used to convey the message of the inscriptions.

In First Order Logic of the inverse property:
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ TX3(x)
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ E56(y)
- TXP6(x,y) ⇒ P2(x,y)
</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="TXP7_has_item">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TXP7 has item</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation>TXP7</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">has item</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="TX13_Script"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="TX8_Grapheme"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="TXP7i_is_item_of"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67_refers_to"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Quantification: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note:
This property associates an instance of TX13 Script with an instance of TX8 Grapheme employed by this script. Different instances of TX13 Script may have some graphemes in common.

Examples:
- The Latin script (TX13) has item the ideal capital letter “S”.

In First Order Logic:
- TXP7(x,y) ⇒ TX3(x)
- TXP7(x,y) ⇒ TX8(y)
</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="TXP7i_is_item_of">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TXP7i is item of</rdfs:label>
