    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="TX8_Grapheme"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="TX13_Script"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="TXP7_has_item"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Quantification of the inverse property: many to many (0,n:0,n)

Scope note of the inverse property:
This property associates an instance of TX13 Script with an instance of TX8 Grapheme employed by this script. Different instances of TX13 Script may have some graphemes in common.

Examples of the inverse property:
- The Latin script (TX13) has item the ideal capital letter “S”.

In First Order Logic of the inverse property:
- TXP7(x,y) ⇒ TX3(x)
- TXP7(x,y) ⇒ TX8(y)
</rdfs:comment>
  </owl:ObjectProperty>
  <owl:ObjectProperty rdf:about="TXP8_has_component">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">TXP8 has component</rdfs:label>
    <skos:notation>TXP8</skos:notation>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">has component</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="TX1_Written_Text"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="TX9_Glyph"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="TXP8i_is_component_of"/>
